  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates><x>1716</x><y>76</y><w>276</w><h>86</h></coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Facade pattern: single entry point
that hides prompt creation, the LLM
client, response parsing and
validation.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates><x>2024</x><y>84</y><w>290</w><h>69</h></coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Factory Method pattern: Creator. Each
subclass decides which LLMPrompt
(Product) to create.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates><x>2346</x><y>67</y><w>276</w><h>103</h></coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Adapter pattern (object adapter):
implements the LLMClient target and
holds the GeminiRestAPI adaptee.
generate() translates a prompt into
generateContent(jsonBody).</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates><x>1386</x><y>76</y><w>298</w><h>86</h></coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Each concrete tool implements all four
Tool methods; only execute() is shown.
Tools wrap services and the facade so
the Planner can invoke them by name.</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
</diagram>
